{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.eigenvalue_product_expansion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eigenvalue_product_expansion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaSym_at_isospin_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaSym_at_isospin_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/eigenvalue_product_expansion.lean#L55-L65","doc":"**Boundary value at `Z = N`** (isospin-symmetric).\nFor `Z = N`, the `q^{(Z−N)(A−1)/2}` factor is `q^0 = 1`, so\n`Λ_sym(Z, Z) = ([2]_q/2)^{Z²}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eigenvalue_product_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eigenvalue_product_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/eigenvalue_product_expansion.lean#L42-L53","doc":"**Closed form of the symmetric-channel eigenvalue product**\n([`prop:eigenvalue-product-expansion`]). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:eigenvalue-product-expansion","label":"prop:eigenvalue-product-expansion","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/eigenvalue-product-expansion.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lambdaSym","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/eigenvalue_product_expansion.lean#L35-L40","doc":"The symmetric-channel eigenvalue product\n`Λ_sym(Z, N) = q^{(Z−N)(A−1)/2} · ([2]_q/2)^{Z·N}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qInt2_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qInt2_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/eigenvalue_product_expansion.lean#L29-L33","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical bracket.** The longhand `q + q⁻¹` is this site's\nbody and its proofs use it, so the consolidation is the identity, not an alias.\nConditional: the two agree away from `q − q⁻¹ = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qInt2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qInt2","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/eigenvalue_product_expansion.lean#L25-L26","doc":"The q-integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}